      <workList xml:id="idm75">
         <work xml:id="work_d1e219216">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_ae5e99e9">A4:Coll.006</identifier>
            <title xml:id="_19" xml:lang="it">Sonate IV–VI a violino solo con basso</title>
            <title type="original" xml:id="title_baaa0342" xml:lang="it">VI Sonate a violino solo con basso, da diversi maestri. Raccolta II</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_91e1e433">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="_20">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <history xml:id="history_21_0">
               <p xml:id="idm84">The collection, comprising six violin sonatas ‘da diversi Maestri’ of which three are by <persName xml:id="idm85" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">Krebs</persName> (presumably Johann Ludwig who was a student of <persName xml:id="idm86" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">Johann Sebastian Bach</persName>'s) and three by Scheibe, has presumably been lost (Krebs' three sonatas are now shelved in <rend xml:id="idm87" fontstyle="italic">D-B</rend>). They are listed in the Breitkopf sales catalogue of 1762 with incipits. The sonatas might have been composed before 1739 when Scheibe briefly mentions having composed solos though without specifying them in greater detail (cf. his autobiography in Mattheson’s <rend xml:id="idm88" fontstyle="italic">Grundlage</rend>, 1740; SchW C5:001). It is likely that Breitkopf obtained the works directly from Scheibe even though they first appear in the catalogue of 1762. At least some of the sonatas might also be listed in the Breitkopf auction catalogue of 1836; the auction lot includes also works by <persName xml:id="idm89" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">Johann Stamitz</persName> and <persName xml:id="idm90" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">Stefano Spadina</persName>.</p>
            </history>
            <langUsage xml:id="langUsage_00be8b88">
               <language xml:id="da">Danish</language>
               <language xml:id="it">Italian</language>
            </langUsage>
            <biblList xml:id="listBibl_7888a492-6a0b-4923-9f17-2b657183fa67255">
               <head xml:id="head_cee1666c">Bibliography</head>
               <bibl label="" xml:id="bibl_d1e263260">
                  <genre xml:id="genre_d9eba377">book</genre>
                  <author xml:id="author_9cfa3d5b">Johann Gottlob Immanuel Breitkopf</author>
                  <annot xml:id="annot_a8d7fe72">
                     <p xml:id="idm100">
                        <lb xml:id="idm101"/>With incipits.</p>
                  </annot>
                  <title level="m" xml:id="title_87b36809">Catalogo dei soli, duetti, [...] e concerti per il violino</title>
                  <title level="s" xml:id="title_0e4d0cdb"/>
                  <biblScope unit="page" xml:id="biblScope_29b1267c">9</biblScope>
                  <imprint xml:id="imprint_bcd05e7f">
                     <date isodate="1762" xml:id="date_7ab369c1">1762</date>
                     <pubPlace xml:id="pubPlace_9ae02956">Leipzig</pubPlace>
